This applet embeds the upstream socat relay engine as an isolated bx applet.

Kept:
- socat's address grammar and relay mechanics
- stdio, fd, file, pipe, UNIX, IPv4/IPv6, TCP, UDP, listen, SOCKS, proxy, and
  text-conversion address support selected by the bx import configuration

Disabled in this first import:
- SYSTEM and SHELL address execution
- EXEC address execution
- OpenSSL, readline, libwrap, syscall tracing, fd analyzer, PTY/termios,
  namespaces, raw IP, tun, SCTP, DCCP, UDP-Lite, VSOCK, and POSIX MQ support

The upstream process-option table still contains privilege-sensitive options
such as `chroot`, `setuid`, and `setsid`; those remain part of the imported
compatibility surface and are reflected in the bx capability classification.

The import config is bx-owned. Unsupported address types must fail closed;
there is no fallback to a shell command or external socat binary.
